## Commands used
Linux commands used for Apache Web Server deployment
No.	Purpose	Command
1	Install Apache HTTP Server	sudo yum install httpd -y
2	Start Apache service	sudo systemctl start httpd
3	Enable Apache service at boot	sudo systemctl enable httpd
4	Switch to root user	sudo su -
5	Create website directory	sudo mkdir -p /var/www/html
6	Create/edit index.html	sudo nano /var/www/html/index.html
7	Check Apache service status	sudo systemctl status httpd
8	Test web server locally	curl -I http://localhost

5. Write HTML content directly into index.html
You can use cat with a heredoc to write the website content:
sudo cat > /var/www/html/index.html <<'EOF'
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My AWS Website</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to my AWS EC2 Website!</h1>
    <p>Hosted on an Amazon Linux instance.</p>
</body>
</html>
EOF


